  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The strongest finding so far is the large multiprofile boost: scvi_n200 goes from 0.520 (singleprofile, config_004) to 0.650 (multiprofile+avgpool, config_005), a +0.13 gain. However, we have only one multiprofile data point, so it is unclear whether this benefit is general across encoders or specific to scvi_n200. config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares against config_001 (pca_n2000, singleprofile) by changing only the profile setting while holding encoder and aggregation fixed. If multiprofile also lifts pca_n2000, it validates multiprofile as a broadly beneficial design axis and justifies further investment (e.g., transformer aggregation in config_006). If it does not, it reveals an encoder×profile interaction that reshapes the search. This single-variable comparison is the most informative next step under a limited budget because it clarifies the scope of the largest effect observed before committing to more complex or expensive extensions."
}

